From 35fbb6b5bece081a2e5a0e1668dc774877940430 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 21:02:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add QR code designer to the admin panel

Adds a "QR" tab where each restaurant can generate and style the QR
that points to its public menu (VMENUS_PUBLIC_URL/slug).

The vendored encoder (qrcode-generator, MIT) only produces the module
matrix; all drawing happens in qr.js so the dots, the three finder
patterns and the centre logo can be styled independently. Shapes are
built once into a backend-neutral list, so the PNG and the SVG export
come out identical without duplicating the drawing logic.

Includes:
- dot and corner styles (square, rounded, circle), independent colours
- transparent background, brand-colour shortcut, adjustable quiet zone
- restaurant logo in the centre, on a plate of the background colour so
  the modules underneath do not blend into it
- A4 poster export with headline, business name and readable link
- PNG (2048px) and SVG (1024px) export
- contrast check that warns on low contrast and on light-on-dark, the
  two cases that silently produce unscannable codes

Error correction switches to H when the logo is on and stays at M
otherwise, which keeps the pattern less dense and easier to scan when
printed small.

Circle dots are drawn tangent (radius = half a module) on purpose:
smaller radii look airier but decoders lose the grid at high
resolution. All 13 style combinations were verified end to end by
rendering in Chromium and decoding with jsQR, including the rasterised
SVG.

The design is stored in restaurantes.atributos.qr, added to the keys a
client role may write.

